<dl id="mwA5Y"><dt id="mwA5c"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt369" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Brazil"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Brazil.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Flag_of_Brazil.svg/40px-Flag_of_Brazil.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/05/Flag_of_Brazil.svg/60px-Flag_of_Brazil.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1000" data-file-height="700" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="22" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazil" title="Brazil" about="#mwt369" id="mwA5k">Brazil</a> (12)</dt>
<dd id="mwA5o">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Marine_Corps" title="Brazilian Marine Corps" id="mwA5s">Brazilian Marine Corps</a> signed a contract for a batch of 12 JLTV in October 2020, to be delivered between 2022 and 2026.<sup about="#mwt370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto1_99-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto1-99" id="mwA5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA50"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA54">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA58">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt373" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-102" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-102"}}'><a href="#cite_note-102" id="mwA6A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6I">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6M">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dd id="mwA6Q">The Brazilian JLTV are equipped with an Objective Gunner Protection Kit and have an Explosively Formed Penetrator (EFP) kit armor suite and a B-kit add-on armor system.<sup about="#mwt376" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_103-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-103"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-103" id="mwA6U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6c">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6g">]</span></span></a></sup> Rumors surfaced in September 2021 regarding a potential purchase of 32 additional JLTVs to equip 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Marine Infantry Battalions and 12 for the Special Operations Battalion, but no additional order has yet taken place.<sup about="#mwt377" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_103-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-103" id="mwA6k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6s">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6w">]</span></span></a></sup> The first delivery of four JLTV took place in March 2023.<sup about="#mwt380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_104-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-104"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-104" id="mwA60"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA64"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA68">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt383" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_105-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-105"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-105" id="mwA7E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA7I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7M">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7Q">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA7U"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV,_August_2024._V.jpeg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA7Y"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV,_August_2024._V.jpeg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV%2C_August_2024._V.jpeg/250px-IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV%2C_August_2024._V.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV%2C_August_2024._V.jpeg/500px-IDF_Oshkosh_JLTV%2C_August_2024._V.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1600" data-file-height="1066" data-file-type="bitmap" height="133" width="200" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.8" id="mwA7c"/></a><figcaption id="mwA7g">A JLTV of the Israel Defense Forces</figcaption></figure>
<dl id="mwA7k"><dt id="mwA7o"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt384" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA7s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Israel"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Israel.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Flag_of_Israel.svg/40px-Flag_of_Israel.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Flag_of_Israel.svg/60px-Flag_of_Israel.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1100" data-file-height="800" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="21" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel" title="Israel" about="#mwt384" id="mwA7w">Israel</a> (≥ 99)</dt>
<dd id="mwA70">In December 2023, Oshkosh announced that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel_Defense_Forces" title="Israel Defense Forces" id="mwA74">Israel Defense Forces</a> ordered 75 JLTV through the Foreign Military Sale (FMS) mechanism, and dozens additional were purchased via Direct Commercial Sale (DCS).<sup about="#mwt387" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-106" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106"}}'><a href="#cite_note-106" id="mwA78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8E">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8I">]</span></span></a></sup> Some JLTV were observed in operation in Israel in November 2024.<sup about="#mwt390" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107"}}'><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwA8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8U">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA8c"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA8g"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg/250px-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg/500px-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicles_of_the_Lithuanian_Armed_Forces_2021-Aug-17_Rukla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1241" data-file-height="827" data-file-type="bitmap" height="133" width="200" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.8" id="mwA8k"/></a><figcaption id="mwA8o">A JLTV of the Lithuanian Armed Forces in Rukla</figcaption></figure>
<dl id="mwA8s"><dt id="mwA8w"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt391" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA80" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lithuania"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lithuania.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Flag_of_Lithuania.svg/40px-Flag_of_Lithuania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Flag_of_Lithuania.svg/60px-Flag_of_Lithuania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1000" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="14" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithuania" title="Lithuania" about="#mwt391" id="mwA84">Lithuania</a> (500)</dt>
<dd id="mwA88">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithuanian_Army" title="Lithuanian Army" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA9A">Lithuanian Army</a> signed a contract for a batch of 200 JLTV in November 2019.<sup about="#mwt394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ArmyTechnology_108-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ArmyTechnology"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ArmyTechnology-108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ArmyTechnology-108" id="mwA9E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9M">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9Q">]</span></span></a></sup> An additional contract for 300 JLTV was signed in October 2022 for a total of 500 vehicles ordered.<sup about="#mwt397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-109" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109"}}'><a href="#cite_note-109" id="mwA9U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9c">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9g">]</span></span></a></sup> The delivery of the first contract was split in 4 batches of 50 vehicles. The first delivery took place in August 2021,<sup about="#mwt400" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110"}}'><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwA9k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9s">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9w">]</span></span></a></sup> the second in December 2022,<sup about="#mwt403" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111"}}'><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwA90"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA94"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA98">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-A">]</span></span></a></sup> the third in May 2023,<sup about="#mwt406" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-112" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-112"}}'><a href="#cite_note-112" id="mwA-E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-M">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-Q">]</span></span></a></sup> and the fourth in December 2023.<sup about="#mwt409" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwA-U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-c">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-g">]</span></span></a></sup>  The delivery of the second contracts is planned for 2024.<sup about="#mwt412" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-114" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-114"}}'><a href="#cite_note-114" id="mwA-k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-s">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-w">]</span></span></a></sup> The variant selected by Lithuania is the M1278A1 with the main equipment being the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CROWS" title="CROWS" id="mwA-0">M153 CROWS v2</a> remote weapon station. This weapon station is equipped with the M2 QCB50 machine gun and a M230 TacFLIR multisensor systems.<sup about="#mwt415" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-115" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-115"}}'><a href="#cite_note-115" id="mwA-4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_A">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_E">]</span></span></a></sup> On 18 February 2026 The Ministry of National Defence has confirmed that all of ordered U.S.-made Joint Light Tactical Vehicles JLTV were delivered to Lithuania in mid-February. The Lithuanian Armed Forces now operates 500 advanced armored vehicles.<sup about="#mwt419" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-116" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-116"}}'><a href="#cite_note-116" id="mwA_I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_Q">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_U">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwA_Y"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt420" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Montenegro"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Montenegro.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Flag_of_Montenegro.svg/40px-Flag_of_Montenegro.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Flag_of_Montenegro.svg/60px-Flag_of_Montenegro.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montenegro" title="Montenegro" about="#mwt420" id="mwA_g">Montenegro</a> (67)</dt>
<dd id="mwA_k">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armed_Forces_of_Montenegro" title="Armed Forces of Montenegro" id="mwA_o">Armed Forces of Montenegro</a> ordered 67 JLTV in October 2019 for US$36.17 million. This order was completed by an order in December 2019 to Elbit for the OCRWS (Overhead Remote Control Weapon Station) weapon station at a cost of US$35 million.<sup about="#mwt423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-117" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-117" id="mwA_s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_0">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_4">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dd id="mwA_8">The variants selected by Montenegro are 55 "M1280 General Purpose" to be fitted with the Elbit weapon station equipped with a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/.50_BMG" title=".50 BMG" id="mwBAA">12.7×99mm NATO</a> heavy machine gun. For the other variants, Montenegro mentions having received 10 "M1278 Heavy Guns Carrier" as of 2024. In 2024, the army announced its interest to equip four of the M1278 variant with a SAMSON 30 (Katlanit) turret. Also, in May 2023, Montenegro signed a contract with Israel for €20 million regarding the supply of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems" title="Elbit Systems" id="mwBAE">Elbit</a> 120 mm Spear Mk2 low recoil mortar systems to be installed on the JLTV (quantity unknown). Those systems are designed to be installed on the M1279 Utility variant, and therefore, with 55 in the M1280 variant and 10 in the M1278 variant, only 2 are possible with the unique order.<sup about="#mwt426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-118" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-118"}}'><a href="#cite_note-118" id="mwBAI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBAM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAQ">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAU">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBAY"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt427" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBAc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"North Macedonia"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Macedonia.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Flag_of_North_Macedonia.svg/40px-Flag_of_North_Macedonia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Flag_of_North_Macedonia.svg/60px-Flag_of_North_Macedonia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Macedonia" title="North Macedonia" about="#mwt427" id="mwBAg">North Macedonia</a> (~97)<sup about="#mwt430" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119"}}'><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwBAk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBAo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAs">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAw">]</span></span></a></sup></dt>
<dd id="mwBA0">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army_of_the_Republic_of_North_Macedonia" title="Army of the Republic of North Macedonia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBA4">Army of the Republic of North Macedonia</a> signed a contract in 2020 for 33 JLTV to be delivered in 2022 and 2023.<sup about="#mwt433" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_120-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:3-120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-120" id="mwBA8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBE">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBI">]</span></span></a></sup> The country has plans for 99 JLTV and options to buy a total of up to 152 JLTV by 2024.<sup about="#mwt436" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-121"}}'><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwBBM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBU">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt437" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_120-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-120" id="mwBBc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBk">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBo">]</span></span></a></sup> In July 2022, the first 6 JLTVs were delivered to the Army, and the rest was delivered by year end of 2022.<sup about="#mwt440" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwBBs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBB0">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBB4">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBB8"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt441" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBCA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Romania"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Romania.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Flag_of_Romania.svg/40px-Flag_of_Romania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Flag_of_Romania.svg/60px-Flag_of_Romania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="600" data-file-height="400" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romania" title="Romania" about="#mwt441" id="mwBCE">Romania</a> (129)</dt>
<dd id="mwBCI">The Romanian government made a Foreign Military Sales request for 34 M1278 Heavy Guns Carrier for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_Special_Operations_Forces_Command" title="Romanian Special Operations Forces Command" id="mwBCM">Romanian Special Operations Forces</a>. This request valued at US$43.73 million was approved by the US Congress and in July 2021, it was announced that a contract was made to supply Romania and other nations with the JLTV.<sup about="#mwt444" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwBCQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBCU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCY">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCc">]</span></span></a></sup> A complementary request was made for 95 additional M1278 HGC valued at US$104 million for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_Land_Forces" title="Romanian Land Forces" id="mwBCg">Romanian Army</a> and was approved by the US Congress in March 2023.<sup about="#mwt447" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwBCk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBCo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCs">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCw">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dd id="mwBC0">Romania received the first 33 JLTVs in November 2023.<sup about="#mwt450" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-125" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-125"}}'><a href="#cite_note-125" id="mwBC4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBC8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDA">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDE">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBDI"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt451" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBDM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Slovenia"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovenia.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Flag_of_Slovenia.svg/40px-Flag_of_Slovenia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Flag_of_Slovenia.svg/60px-Flag_of_Slovenia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovenia" title="Slovenia" about="#mwt451" id="mwBDQ">Slovenia</a> (129)</dt>
<dd id="mwBDU">Slovenia Ministry of Defense signed a Letter of Offer and Acceptance (LOA) with the U.S. government in October 2018 for the purchase of 38 JLTV (local designation: LKOV) in the M1278 Heavy Guns Carrier variant.<sup about="#mwt454" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwBDY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDg">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDk">]</span></span></a></sup> The order to Oshkosh by the U.S. government was announced in February 2020.<sup about="#mwt455" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto1_99-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto1-99" id="mwBDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDw">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBD0">]</span></span></a></sup> The delivery of this batch took place at the port of Luka Koper in May 2021.<sup about="#mwt458" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-127" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-127"}}'><a href="#cite_note-127" id="mwBD4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBD8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEA">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEE">]</span></span></a></sup> At that time, the minister of defense announced an interest for 99 additional JLTV. Regarding the equipment, all are to be equipped with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CROWS" title="CROWS" id="mwBEI">Kongsberg M153 CROWS</a> remote weapon station. These are fitted with a M2 machine gun and capable to shoot the Spike LR and Spike LR2 which are in service in the Slovenian Army.<sup about="#mwt461" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"}}'><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwBEM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEU">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEY">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2021, Slovenia Ministry of Defense signed an agreement with the U.S. Government for the purchase of 37 JLTV.<sup about="#mwt462" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto1_99-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto1-99" id="mwBEc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEk">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEo">]</span></span></a></sup> The delivery of this batch took place in December 2023.<sup about="#mwt465" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_129-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-auto-129"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-129" id="mwBEs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBE0">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBE4">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2022, another order for 47 vehicles obtained via direct commercial sale was placed in the same variant, with a delivery planned for 2024.<sup about="#mwt466" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_129-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-129" id="mwBE8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFE">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFI">]</span></span></a></sup> The US will also donate 7 JLTV.<sup about="#mwt469" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-130" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-130" id="mwBFM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFU">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFY">]</span></span></a></sup> As of January 2024, 75 JLTV were delivered, and 54 additional are to be delivered. The plan is to reach a total fleet of 161 JLTV.<sup about="#mwt470" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_129-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-129" id="mwBFc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFk">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFo">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBFs"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt471" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBFw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"United States"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Flag_of_the_United_States.svg/40px-Flag_of_the_United_States.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Flag_of_the_United_States.svg/60px-Flag_of_the_United_States.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1235" data-file-height="650" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" about="#mwt471" id="mwBF0">United States</a> (approx. 19,150 delivered, all U.S. Army orders are cancelled,<sup about="#mwt474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwBF4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBF8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGA">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGE">]</span></span></a></sup> USMC is still ordering.<sup about="#mwt477" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwBGI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGQ">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGU">]</span></span></a></sup>)</dt>
<dd id="mwBGY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Army" title="U.S. Army" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBGc">U.S. Army</a> (estimated 15,000 as of January 2025<sup about="#mwt481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Military_Balance_2025_133-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Military Balance 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Military_Balance_2025-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Military_Balance_2025-133" id="mwBGg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGo">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt478" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBGw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"rp","href":"./Template:Rp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"36"}},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Page / location: 36"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>36<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Marine_Corps" title="U.S. Marine Corps" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBG0">U.S. Marine Corps</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Air_Force" title="U.S. Air Force" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBG4">U.S. Air Force</a> – Original contract award in August 2015. Overall requirements have fluctuated, but as of January 2022 were stated by Michael Sprang, JLTV Project Director to be 49,099 for the Army; approximately 12,500 for the Marine Corps; 2,000 for the Air Force (dependent on funding); and approximately 400 for the Navy. The initial JLTV contract award had a potential value of US$6.749 billion and called for a maximum of 16,901 JLTV. The second sole source to Oshkosh contract allows for 6,262 JLTV to be ordered by November 2023. The JLTV re-compete award will allow for 15,586 JLTV when awarded. Current U.S. Army and Marines orders are for around 19,150 JLTV.<sup about="#mwt484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwBG8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHE">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt488" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135"}}'><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwBHM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHU">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt489" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle_(JLTV)_(March_2022_updates)_8-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Joint Light Tactical Vehicle (JLTV) (March 2022 updates)"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle_(JLTV)_(March_2022_updates)-8" id="mwBHc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHk">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHo">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwBHs" aria-labelledby="Future_operators"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Future_operators">Future operators</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: Future operators"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<dl id="mwBHw"><dt id="mwBH0"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt490" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBH4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Mongolia"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mongolia.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Mongolia.svg/40px-Flag_of_Mongolia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Mongolia.svg/60px-Flag_of_Mongolia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongolia" title="Mongolia" about="#mwt490" id="mwBH8">Mongolia</a> (unknown quantity)</dt>
<dd id="mwBIA">In November 2023, it is mentioned in official documents that JLTV were ordered by the US for Foreign Military Sales to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongolian_Ground_Force" title="Mongolian Ground Force" id="mwBIE">Mongolian Army</a>. No mention of the quantity, or the price of the order is made in the document.<sup about="#mwt493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-136" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136"}}'><a href="#cite_note-136" id="mwBII"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIQ">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIU">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBIY"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt494" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBIc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Uruguay"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Uruguay.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Flag_of_Uruguay.svg/40px-Flag_of_Uruguay.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Flag_of_Uruguay.svg/60px-Flag_of_Uruguay.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="341" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uruguay" title="Uruguay" about="#mwt494" id="mwBIg">Uruguay</a> (20)</dt>
<dd id="mwBIk">In May 2023, a specialized Spanish defense website announced that the United States government approved the transfer of 20 JLTV to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uruguayan_Armed_Forces" title="Uruguayan Armed Forces" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBIo">Armed Forces of Uruguay</a> with Global Peace Operations Initiative (GPOI) funds.<sup about="#mwt498" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwBIs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI0">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI4">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_lacking_reliable_references" about="#mwt495" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBI8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Better source","href":"./Template:Better_source"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"This is over a year old and no better sources in English available yet?"},"date":{"wt":"May 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_lacking_reliable_references_from_May_2024" about="#mwt495"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template noprint noexcerpt Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt495" id="mwBJA"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Questionable_sources" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability"><span title="This claim needs references to better sources. (May 2024)">better<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>source<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBJE"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt499" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBJI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Slovakia"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovakia.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Flag_of_Slovakia.svg/40px-Flag_of_Slovakia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Flag_of_Slovakia.svg/60px-Flag_of_Slovakia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovakia" title="Slovakia" about="#mwt499" id="mwBJM">Slovakia</a> (160)</dt>
<dd id="mwBJQ">The Slovak Defence Ministry announced its interest for the acquisition of 180 JLTV in the M1278A1 Heavy Gun Carrier variant in March 2023, using a grant of €200 million from the United States. In May 2023, the US State Department approved the sale of up to 192 vehicles for US$250 million.<sup about="#mwt502" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwBJU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJc">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJg">]</span></span></a></sup> In July 2023, the Slovak Defence Ministry accepted the offer for 160 JLTV for US$190 million through the FMF grant (Foreign Military Financing). Some of the JLTV are to be equipped with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CROWS" title="CROWS" id="mwBJk">Kongsberg M153 CROWS</a> remote station, and some with a manned weapon station. The deliveries are due to take place in 2025.<sup about="#mwt505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwBJo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJw">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJ0">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBJ4"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt506" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBJ8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Netherlands"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg/40px-Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg/60px-Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands" title="Netherlands" about="#mwt506" id="mwBKA">Netherlands</a> (> 150)</dt>
<dd id="mwBKE">150 Oshkosh JLTV ordered in April 2025 by the Netherlands MOD for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Netherlands_Marine_Corps" title="Royal Netherlands Marine Corps" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBKI">Royal Netherlands Marine Corps</a> as part of the FLATM-PV programme (Future Littoral All Terrain Mobility – Patrol Vehicle). The vehicle will be known as the DXPV (Dutch Expeditionary Patrol Vehicles) and in Dutch service will be named Kaaiman.<sup about="#mwt509" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-140" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-140" id="mwBKM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKU">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKY">]</span></span></a></sup> 
<ul id="mwBKc"><li id="mwBKg">First contract: signed in June 2025<sup about="#mwt512" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-141" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-141" id="mwBKk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKs">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKw">]</span></span></a></sup>, with deliveries expected to start in 2028.<sup about="#mwt515" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-142" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-142" id="mwBK0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBK4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBK8">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt518" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143"}}'><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwBLE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLM">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt521" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-144" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-144"}}'><a href="#cite_note-144" id="mwBLU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLc">[</span>144<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBLk">Second contract: complementary order in January 2026, worth €23.0 to 28.0 million.<sup about="#mwt524" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-145" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-145"}}'><a href="#cite_note-145" id="mwBLo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLw">[</span>145<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></dd>
<dt id="mwBL4"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt525" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBL8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Canada"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Canada_(Pantone).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/40px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/60px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada" title="Canada" about="#mwt525" id="mwBMA">Canada</a> (60)</dt>
<dd id="mwBME">In August 2025, the U.S. State Department approved a $160M US <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Military_Sales" title="Foreign Military Sales" id="mwBMI">Foreign Military Sale</a> of 60 JLTVs to be accompanied by 9 JLTV cargo trailers, as well as communication equipment and other hardware.<sup about="#mwt528" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-146" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-146"}}'><a href="#cite_note-146" id="mwBMM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMU">[</span>146<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMY">]</span></span></a></sup> The vehicles would replace <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Special_Operations_Forces_Command" title="Canadian Special Operations Forces Command" id="mwBMc">CANSOFCOM</a>'s fleet of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humvee" title="Humvee" id="mwBMg">HMMWV</a> under the Next Generation Fighting Vehicle project.<sup about="#mwt531" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-147" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147"}}'><a href="#cite_note-147" id="mwBMk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMs">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMw">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwBM0" aria-labelledby="Potential_operators"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Potential_operators">Potential operators</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: Potential operators"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<dl id="mwBM4"><dt id="mwBM8"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt532" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBNA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Greece"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Greece.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Flag_of_Greece.svg/40px-Flag_of_Greece.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Flag_of_Greece.svg/60px-Flag_of_Greece.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="600" data-file-height="400" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greece" title="Greece" about="#mwt532" id="mwBNE">Greece</a> (unknown quantity)</dt>
<dd id="mwBNI">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenic_Army" title="Hellenic Army" id="mwBNM">Hellenic Army</a> mentioned the potential purchase of JLTV to be equipped with various equipments as an option:
<ul id="mwBNQ"><li id="mwBNU">In June 2022, the Hellenic Army General Staff met with representatives from Elbit Systems after showing interest in the acquisition of SPEAR 120mm mortar systems mounted on the JLTV.<sup about="#mwt535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-148" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-148"}}'><a href="#cite_note-148" id="mwBNY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNg">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-149" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-149"}}'><a href="#cite_note-149" id="mwBNo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNw">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBN0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBN4">In April 2023, the Hellenic Army ordered <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spike_(missile)" title="Spike (missile)" id="mwBN8">Spike</a> missiles for €370 million. As part of the variants ordered, Greece mentions the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spike_(missile)#Spike_NLOS" title="Spike (missile)" id="mwBOA">Spike NLOS</a>. In its terrestrial use, it would be installed on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasan_SandCat" title="Plasan SandCat" id="mwBOE">Plasan SandCat</a> or the JLTV.<sup about="#mwt541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-150" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150"}}'><a href="#cite_note-150" id="mwBOI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOQ">[</span>150<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOU">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></dd>
<dt id="mwBOY"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt542" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBOc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Poland"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Poland.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Flag_of_Poland.svg/40px-Flag_of_Poland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Flag_of_Poland.svg/60px-Flag_of_Poland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1280" data-file-height="800" data-file-type="drawing" height="14" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poland" title="Poland" about="#mwt542" id="mwBOg">Poland</a> (26)</dt>
<dd id="mwBOk">In December 2022, U.S. Congress approved the sale of 26 M1279A1 JLTV to Poland as part of a package of military sales to Poland.<sup about="#mwt545" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-151" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-151"}}'><a href="#cite_note-151" id="mwBOo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOw">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBO0">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2023, the order of the 116 M1A1 was confirmed, with this confirmation, 12 M88A2, 8 M1110, 6 M577 and 26 M1152A1 workshop <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humvee" title="Humvee" id="mwBO4">Humvees</a> was confirmed with their logistic package, but no mention of the JLTV.<sup about="#mwt548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-152" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-152"}}'><a href="#cite_note-152" id="mwBO8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPE">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPI">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBPM"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt549" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBPQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Portugal"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(official).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Flag_of_Portugal_%28official%29.svg/40px-Flag_of_Portugal_%28official%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Flag_of_Portugal_%28official%29.svg/60px-Flag_of_Portugal_%28official%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portugal" title="Portugal" about="#mwt549" id="mwBPU">Portugal</a> (230 planned)</dt>
<dd id="mwBPY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_Army" title="Portuguese Army" id="mwBPc">Portuguese Army</a> – In April 2020, Portugal announced that it would be seeking to procure the JLTV through the US Foreign Military Sales program. The intention was expressed to Janes by Lieutenant Colonel Ricardo Manuel dos Santos Camilo, head of the capabilities branch of the army general staff's force planning division. In 2019, EUR79 million (US$86 million) was allocated to the revised Portuguese Military Programming Law for the acquisition of the JLTV by 2030 for further army modernisation. The total procurement was under review and it was stated that it could change. If purchased, the JLTV would replace the Land Rover Defender series and the Toyota Land Cruiser HZJ73LV vehicles used by the Portuguese Army.<sup about="#mwt552" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153"}}'><a href="#cite_note-153" id="mwBPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPo">[</span>153<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto1_99-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto1-99" id="mwBPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP4">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP8">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023, it was reported that 230 JLTVs are to be procured.<sup about="#mwt556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-154" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154"}}'><a href="#cite_note-154" id="mwBQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQI">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQM">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBQQ"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt557" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBQU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"United Kingdom"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(1-2).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281-2%29.svg/40px-Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281-2%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281-2%29.svg/60px-Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281-2%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom" title="United Kingdom" about="#mwt557" id="mwBQY">United Kingdom</a> (up to 2,747)</dt>
<dd id="mwBQc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Army" title="British Army" id="mwBQg">British Army</a> – In June 2016 it was reported that to meet Package 1 of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi_Role_Vehicle-Protected" title="Multi Role Vehicle-Protected" id="mwBQk">Multi Role Vehicle-Protected</a> (MRV-P) requirement, the UK <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Defence_(United_Kingdom)" title="Ministry of Defence (United Kingdom)" id="mwBQo">Ministry of Defence</a> (MoD) was in talks with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pentagon" title="The Pentagon" id="mwBQs">the Pentagon</a> on acquiring the JLTV via the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Military_Sales" title="Foreign Military Sales" id="mwBQw">Foreign Military Sales</a> (FMS) route. “We can confirm that we are talking to the US DOD regarding Package 1 [of MRV-P], to inform our understanding of an FMS option for the Joint Light Tactical Vehicle,” said an MoD spokesman.<sup about="#mwt560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-155" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-155"}}'><a href="#cite_note-155" id="mwBQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQ8">[</span>155<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRA">]</span></span></a></sup> It was stated in January 2017 by Maj. Gen. Robert Talbot Rice, the director of land equipment at the Defence Equipment and Support arm of the Ministry of Defence (MoD), that: "We are working through the Foreign Military Sales process. A letter of request has been sent to our American colleagues, and we expect a response in the next few months." Talbot Rice told an audience of industry executives and military personnel at the International Armoured Vehicles conference in London on 24 January that the Army had opted for the single-source purchase due to its ability to meet UK requirements and its value for money.<sup about="#mwt563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-156" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-156"}}'><a href="#cite_note-156" id="mwBRE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRM">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In July 2017, the DSCA notified the US Congress of a possible sale of 2,747 JLTV vehicles and accessories to the UK.<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-157" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-157"}}'><a href="#cite_note-157" id="mwBRU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRc">[</span>157<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt567" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle_(JLTV)_(Sept_2017_updates)2_53-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Joint Light Tactical Vehicle (JLTV) (Sept 2017 updates)2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle_(JLTV)_(Sept_2017_updates)2-53" id="mwBRk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRs">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRw">]</span></span></a></sup> Jane's Defence Weekly reported in September 2019 that approval for the JLTV to enter the demonstration phase was received in April 2019 and that once the demonstration phase was complete in 2021, a new business case would be submitted to the MoD for approval to enter full rate production. The requirement at that time stood at 821 vehicles for the Army and Marines.<sup about="#mwt570" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-158" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-158"}}'><a href="#cite_note-158" id="mwBR0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBR4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBR8">[</span>158<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSA">]</span></span></a></sup> In June 2022, it was announced that the Package 1 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi_Role_Vehicle-Protected" title="Multi Role Vehicle-Protected" id="mwBSE">Multi Role Vehicle-Protected</a> (MRV-P) requirement purchase would not move forward; cancellation of the MRV-P Package 1 is not a direct cancellation of the JLTV acquisition, and actually a result of the British Army reviewing its protected mobility needs after the 2021 Integrated Review and associated Command Paper. Delaying any JLTV purchase will also allow the UK to await the outcome of the US Army JLTV recompete process.<sup about="#mwt573" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-159" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-159"}}'><a href="#cite_note-159" id="mwBSI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSQ">[</span>159<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSU">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwBSY" aria-labelledby="Evaluation_only"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Evaluation_only">Evaluation only</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Joint_Light_Tactical_Vehicle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25" title="Edit section: Evaluation only"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<dl id="mwBSc"><dt id="mwBSg"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt574" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBSk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Australia"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Australia_(converted).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg/40px-Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg/60px-Flag_of_Australia_%28converted%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1280" data-file-height="640" data-file-type="drawing" height="12" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia" title="Australia" about="#mwt574" id="mwBSo">Australia</a></dt>
<dd id="mwBSs">As part of the program <i id="mwBSw">Project Land 121 Phase 4 – Protected Mobility Vehicle (Light) (PMV-L)</i>, Australia evaluated several options, among which, the possibility to purchase the JLTV that was being developed by the USA. In the end, the Thales <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawkei" title="Hawkei" id="mwBS0">Hawkei</a> won the competition.<sup about="#mwt577" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-160" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-160"}}'><a href="#cite_note-160" id="mwBS4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBS8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTA">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTE">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
<dt id="mwBTI"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt578" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBTM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Japan"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Japan.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9e/Flag_of_Japan.svg/40px-Flag_of_Japan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9e/Flag_of_Japan.svg/60px-Flag_of_Japan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan" title="Japan" about="#mwt578" id="mwBTQ">Japan</a></dt>
<dd id="mwBTU">Japan was looking for a successor of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komatsu_LAV" title="Komatsu LAV" id="mwBTY">Komatsu LAV</a>. The JLTV was one of the competitors, but only the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mowag_Eagle" title="Mowag Eagle" id="mwBTc">Mowag Eagle V</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawkei" title="Hawkei" id="mwBTg">Thales Hawkei</a> were pre-selected for evaluation.<sup about="#mwt581" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-161" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161"}}'><a href="#cite_note-161" id="mwBTk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTs">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-162" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162"}}'><a href="#cite_note-162" id="mwBT0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBT4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT8">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUA">]</span></span></a></sup></dd></dl>

